Official LaaS Velocity Communicator.

Version: 0.12.2
API: 25.3.0

Author: Velocity Support

Email: velocity.support@nokia.com

Quick start guide and documentation:
https://nokia.sharepoint.com/sites/lms/SitePages/Instructions.aspx

Velocity API documentation:
https://velocityoulu.ou.nsn-rdnet.net/velocity/api/doc/

More information about Velocity you can find from LaaS homepage:
https://nokia.sharepoint.com/sites/lms/SitePages/Home.aspx

Bug reports, feature suggestions and support requests:
https://jiradc.ext.net.nokia.com/projects/VELOCITY

Artifactory package:
https://artifactory-espoo1.int.net.nokia.com/ui/repos/tree/General/mn-velocity-communicator-local

1. Installation

    1. Change directory to main project folder.
    2. pip install .

    All dependencies will be installed along with package.

2. Notice (velocity.support@nokia.com):

    * Using Python3 for the developing.
    * Tested in Windows.
    * This code is 'under development' version.

3. How to use it:

        from velocity_communicator import velocityclient
        
        CLIENT = velocityclient.VelocityRestClient(<velocity_ip>, <login>, <password>)

        print (CLIENT.get_server_time())

4. Documentation generator:

    For Windows users:
        Documentation for the project is generated by Sphinx. To generate it, change directory to 'docs' and run 'make.bat html' (to generate html documentation) or 'make.bat latex' (to generate latex files). Run 'make_pdf.bat' to generate pdf file (there must(!) be an actual latex build in docs/build/latex)

5. Links:
    Velocity REST API documentation https://velocityoulu.ou.nsn-rdnet.net/velocity/api/doc/

6. External libraries:
    * requests,
    * beautifulsoup4,
    * six,
    * yaml

7. External libraries for documentation
    * sphinx, sphinxcontrib-napoleon

    MiKTex distribution is required to generate documentation in pdf format.
